Parent roadmap: #890

Provider context: #893 / #916

## Outcome

Make the public IndexedDB filesystem boundary reject requested semantics it does not advertise instead of silently weakening them.

## Changes

- add a public IndexedDB provider wrapper around the raw transactional storage implementation;
- reject `copy(..., {preserveModified: true})` with `file/unsupported` before a transaction starts;
- reject `move(..., {atomic: true})` with `file/unsupported` before a transaction starts;
- retain provider diagnostics through `preserve-modified-unavailable` and `atomic-move-unavailable` codes;
- route `hara-web.js`, the Kernel-context host adapter and real-Chromium conformance through the guarded factory;
- add focused fake-IndexedDB tests proving rejected operations create no target and leave the source unchanged;
- add the guard and capability test to permanent IndexedDB CI and the Studio test command.

## Validation

The final one-commit branch passed its authoritative provider matrix:

- **IndexedDB Filesystem CI / Node and fake IndexedDB:** success;
- **IndexedDB Filesystem CI / Real Chromium IndexedDB:** success;
- **Core CI:** success;
- **Pong canvas runtime:** success;
- **Native, protocol, and Foundation behavioral conformance in browser Wasm:** success.

The focused commands exercised by the permanent workflow are:

```text
cd core/rust/web
npm ci
node --check host/indexeddb-filesystem-provider.js
node --check indexeddb-filesystem-capabilities.test.mjs
node --test \
  indexeddb-filesystem.test.mjs \
  indexeddb-filesystem-capabilities.test.mjs \
  indexeddb-filesystem-host.test.mjs \
  indexeddb-provider-services.test.mjs \
  hara-web.test.mjs
npx playwright test indexeddb-filesystem-browser.spec.js
```

## Existing repository-wide blocker

The broader Whole-Wasm suite fails in three unrelated Rust tests before exercising this JavaScript-only provider change:

- `selects_forward_and_natural_regions_but_keeps_nested_loop_fallback` — unsupported `BuiltinValue 3`;
- `arithmetic_errors_match_hara_semantics` — whole-Wasm value/integer overflow mismatch;
- `recursive_array_parameters_keep_their_linear_memory_representation` — unsupported `BuiltinValue 2`.

This PR changes no Rust source or Whole-Wasm fixture. Its Core, IndexedDB, Chromium and browser-Wasm checks are green.

## Boundaries

- no capability is newly advertised;
- no storage schema or transaction implementation changes;
- no public `std.native.File` operation changes;
- no raw-Wasm host migration is included;
- no SFTP, GitHub credential or Google Drive work is included.

Advances #890.

