## Validation target

Add an implementation-independent regression oracle for the central J1 state solver.

For 96 deterministic small finite contracts (1–4 worlds), the test:

- generates four audit contracts with varying static distinctions, legal-action rows, and successors;
- enumerates **every partition** of the carrier;
- checks common-fixed-point validity directly from audit semantics without calling `AuditRefinement.close`;
- independently selects the unique coarsest admissible partition above the baseline;
- compares that oracle result with `solve_joint_crest_state`;
- repeats with reversed audit order;
- independently checks full-state and target-only evidence licensing.

## Why this matters

The existing J1 theorem is analytic and the seven-world witness already checks a noncommuting case. This PR adds broad regression protection against implementation drift in the solver itself, without changing the theorem or scientific claims.

## Scope

One test file only. No theorem implementation, manuscript, or claim changes.

## Scope
Production-freeze CP05D follow-up: make bundled category icon resolution reliable on Linux and guard the catalog asset directory against case-only ambiguity.

### Gap
Category names are normalized to lowercase slugs, but bundled assets may retain uppercase characters (for example `SSC-CGL.png`). The previous resolver synthesized lowercase filenames and checked them with `existsSync`, so Linux deployments could miss a real asset and fall back to a generic icon.

### Production change
- index actual files in each category-icon root;
- match requested slug+extension case-insensitively;
- return the real on-disk filename casing in `/category-icons/...` URLs;
- cache each directory index to avoid rescanning for every category row;
- fail closed if two supported icon assets collide case-insensitively;
- preserve extension priority and the existing `currentIcon` fallback contract.

### Deterministic guard
`audit:startup-performance` expands from 89 to 99 assertions and now verifies:
- the category icon asset directory is non-empty;
- no case-insensitive filename collisions exist;
- SSC-CGL and Punjab assets are addressable by normalized slugs;
- resolver uses actual directory filenames, normalized lookup keys, collision detection, actual-case URLs and caching.

### Release gate
Do not merge unless the exact PR head executes and passes:
- Student TypeScript
- Frontend production quality
- Render production build
- Student reliability E2E

No runner/auth/catalog API contract or frontend rendering behavior is intentionally changed.

## M6D2 — CEI merchandising v1

Closes the merchandising half of M6D without changing the public storefront contract.

### What changes
- adds a bounded, source-neutral `CEI_MERCHANDISING_CONTRACT_VERSION=1`;
- attaches merchandising metadata to the generic Knowledge Pack contract;
- moves the Sports navigation definition out of legacy `catalog-normalization.js` and into Sports Knowledge Pack v1;
- preserves `professionalNavigationDefinition()` only as a compatibility adapter over the pack;
- materializes tenant navigation from actual classified entity/facet counts;
- persists public-safe `catalog_meta.navigation` plus internal versioned `catalog_meta.merchandising`;
- classification only completes after merchandising persistence succeeds;
- uses tenant-native `TENANT_DISPATCH` path for those D1 reads/writes;
- adds a non-Sports `test-wheels-v1` pack proving the merchandising Core does not depend semantically on football;
- adds fallback pack navigation only when every resolved count is still zero, avoiding an empty storefront explorer.

### Invariants
- no supplier/provenance/source URLs in public navigation;
- SOURCE INFERENCE + MERCHANT OVERRIDE remains unchanged;
- Sports remains a Knowledge Pack, not the CEI Core;
- no second provider, universal research or redesign in this slice;
- public API remains backward-compatible.

### Gate
Merge only after all secret-free PR checks pass. After trusted-main deploy, require fresh automatic canary success before declaring M6D2 production-green.

## Mission
Repair the first exact-head executable gate failure without changing poker answer keys, and reduce Actions waste on future static failures.

## Root cause
`decisions-recognition-expansion.ts` helper required separate RU/EN rationale arguments, while the authored A5 corpus uses one source-backed rationale and optionally passes `changedVariables` in the next slot. Exact-head CI reached the runner and failed at TypeScript before build/E2E.

## Repair
- make the recognition helper backward-compatible with one rationale, bilingual rationale, and optional changed variables;
- preserve all decision IDs, sources, correct actions/reasons and changed-node semantics;
- run `npm test` before Playwright browser provisioning;
- run E2E only after static gate passes;
- avoid secondary visual-artifact failure when a static gate stops before screenshots can exist.

## Validation
No GREEN claim on this branch. Merge into the program branch, then use the automatically triggered PR #87 exact-head validation as the authoritative gate.

