Adds the ability to [configure project tracing settings](https://vercel.com/changelog/always-on-tracing-for-production-and-preview-traffic) via Terraform provider.

Example

```
resource "vercel_project" "example" {
  name = "example"
}

resource "vercel_project_tracing" "example" {
  project_id = vercel_project.example.id

  sampling_rules = [{
    rate         = 0.2
    environment  = "production"
    request_path = "/api"
  }]
}
```

Deleting the resource disables tracing for the project. An empty or omitted `sampling_rules` array means no filter is applied and 100% traces are retained.

Maintenance-only correctness pass from the latest private production review. No Smart authority expansion and no v1.2.5 feature yet.

Scope:
- share canonical metadata/title classification between Standard and Smart while preserving Standard TXT/untimed support;
- make documented Smart/Pro CLI entry points bootstrap from repository root without PYTHONPATH;
- keep Pro v1.1.3 internal full-pool planning but report the caller-requested primary max_jobs budget truthfully;
- add synthetic regressions only; no private song/cue/timestamp/BPM data.

Smart v1.2.4 remains the production default. The A-bounded v1.2.5 candidate is intentionally deferred until this corrected baseline is rerun on private production data.

## Restored working baseline

V1.4.1 is restored as the active Candidate baseline after the V1.4.2/V1.4.3 storage/launcher experiments were rejected in real-device validation.

This branch keeps the last known-good architecture:
- Vite build is a complete runnable client under `app/`;
- the current built-in Lanzhou map remains part of the client build;
- Server serves only `app/` as the web client;
- portable runtime persistence remains under `map/` (`world.json`, `users.json`, `uploads/`, `backups/`);
- Player Identity / Player Key / Actor Ownership / Combat Turn Lock remain intact.

The `map/` folder name is semantically imperfect, but it is intentionally preserved for this rollback rather than mixing a storage migration into recovery.

## Next architecture direction

Future launcher/world/scene work will be redesigned around a Foundry-style rule:
- one Server owns the disk Data Path;
- browser Client knows only HTTP/WebSocket URLs, never filesystem paths;
- Launcher starts/stops the Server and consumes management/status APIs only;
- Scene/World persistence belongs to World data;
- no separate external `maps/` source will be introduced until Scene Manager is implemented end-to-end.

This PR remains Draft while the exact V1.4.1 package is revalidated on Windows.

