## Purpose

Replace the remaining `workflow_run.pull_requests[]` dependency in privileged AI-index provider maintenance with exact branch-based PR resolution on current master.

## Security boundary

- `workflow_run` remains the post-Build privilege-separation path; no `pull_request_target:synchronize` trigger is added;
- the gate is checkout-free, secret-free and read-only with `pull-requests: read`;
- completed Build must be a `pull_request` event with same-repository canonical head SHA and non-empty head branch;
- GitHub Pull Requests API must resolve that owner branch to exactly one open PR;
- repository owner, same repository and exact current head SHA are independently rechecked;
- exact `/refresh-ai-index <sha> CONFIRM_OPENROUTER_REAL_EMBEDDING_RUN` remains mandatory before provider work;
- ambiguity or stale authority is a successful unauthorized no-op, not a widened trust path.

The two-file change is the previously reviewed #307 hardening, re-applied without force-rewriting the stale branch onto master `677d129c2c8272629b5bd26c213fd9a91cd20739`.

